UPDATE tarot_cards 
SET meaning_upright = 'GENERAL ARCHETYPE: The Three of Cups represents the absolute archetype of communal ecstasy, the celebratory expansion of the emotional field from a dyad into a triad, and the emergence of the collective consciousness as a primary driver of joy and creative fruition. Moving beyond the intimate, mirrored reflection of the Two, the Three of Cups signifies the phase where energy is no longer just exchanged; it is amplified through the sacred geometry of the circle. This is the "harvest" phase of the emotional suit, where the seeds of intention planted in the Ace and nurtured in the Two now blossom into a shared experience of triumph, creative synthesis, and lighthearted, high-frequency communion. In this state, your individual psychic frequency is augmented by the presence of a supportive network, creating a "collective resonance" that lifts the baseline of all participants. Visually depicted as three figures raising their chalices high, the card symbolizes the elevation of the mundane into the sacred through the lens of shared experience and spiritual kinship. It is a profound acknowledgment that joy is a multiplier—a force that, when shared, does not deplete the individual source but rather revitalizes it through the recursive feedback loops of mutual validation and collective creative spark. This archetype speaks to an exceptional phase where your greatest assets are your ability to integrate into a supportive tribe, your capacity to recognize the divine spark in others as a reflection of your own, and your courage to celebrate the manifest results of your long-term emotional labor. It commands you to step out of the isolated, egoic silos of the past and recognize that your success is inherently tethered to the quality of your community. To inhabit the Three of Cups is to master the alchemy of social grace, transforming the raw, potentially chaotic energy of human interaction into a stable, radiant field of support that acts as a secure platform for your next, more ambitious cycle of growth. It is the ultimate cosmic validation that you are not walking this path alone, and that the universe supports your journey by surrounding you with mirrors of your own highest potential.',
meaning_reversed = 'GENERAL ARCHETYPE: When the Three of Cups appears in the reversed position, it acts as a severe, high-amplitude diagnostic signal of systemic fragmentation within your social and emotional architecture—a "de-synced" state where the celebratory energy of the triad has curdled into exclusionary friction, social performance, or the bitter decay of a shared dream. This reversal marks the phase where the feedback loops of your community have turned toxic, converting the once-uplifting resonance into a feedback loop of gossip, performative belonging, or the gnawing isolation that comes from being surrounded by others while remaining fundamentally unseen. The elevated chalices are now perceived as barriers; the circle has been broken by egoic competition, cliquishness, or the cold, hard realization that the "community" you have built is resting on a foundation of shallow, low-vibration artifice rather than authentic soul-recognition. From an analytical perspective, this is a clear sign that you are leaking massive amounts of vital processing energy into the maintenance of a social narrative that no longer serves your internal evolutionary trajectory. You may find yourself trapped in the "echo chamber" of your own social scripts, terrified that if you drop the act, the connections you have cultivated will dissolve entirely. The reversed Three of Cups exposes the hidden fissures in your tribal structure: the unvoiced competition, the performative intimacy, and the profound lack of genuine reciprocal support that characterizes your current interactions. This reversal commands an immediate and radical audit of your relational variables: you are being asked to identify exactly where you are sacrificing your personal integrity to fit into a collective that does not truly understand your path. This is a call to stop the performative drain, to pull your energy back from these discordant, high-entropy connections, and to courageously sit with the uncomfortable silence of your own company. You must dismantle the false facade of the "perfect social life" and initiate a deep, thorough purge of the relationships that act as a drag on your spiritual evolution. It is a demand to return to the root of your own sovereign truth, acknowledging that it is far better to stand alone in your integrity than to participate in a collective illusion that leaves your heart feeling profoundly starved, misunderstood, and fundamentally misaligned with the high-frequency intent you are attempting to manifest.'
WHERE id = 3;
